  "question": {
    "text": "A plane passing through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> contains two lines whose direction ratios are<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math>and<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></math> respectively. If, this plane also passes through the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Plane is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Direction ratios of lines are<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Since both lines lie in to the plane implies dot product of direction ratios&nbsp;of line with direction ratio of normal of plane will be zero.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>a</mi></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>4</mn></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>b</mi></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>c</mi></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mstyle></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Direction ratios&nbsp;of normal of plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Equation of plane is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> lies on plane</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p>"
  }
